        "original_id": "e96f9029-545a-5c64-b0d4-a45096f11606",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Judy Clarke, Eric Rudolph, Ted Kaczynski, Jared Lee Loughner, Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, Tamerlan Tsarnaev\n- Roles: defense attorney, domestic terrorist\n- Events: plea agreements, anti-abortion and anti-gay bombings, Trial of Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, Boston Marathon bombing, murder of an MIT police officer\n\nFacts:\n- Between 1996 and 1998, Eric Rudolph carried out anti-abortion and anti-gay-motivated bombings across the southern United States.\n- Eric Rudolph was born on September 19, 1966, and is also known as the Olympic Park Bomber.\n- Eric Rudolph is an American domestic terrorist convicted for bombings that killed two people and injured more than 120 others.\n- Judy Clarke has negotiated plea agreements that spared her clients the death penalty in the cases of Eric Rudolph, Ted Kaczynski, and Jared Lee Loughner.\n- During the Trial of Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, Judy Clarke told jurors that Dzhokhar Tsarnaev and his older brother Tamerlan planted a bomb that killed three people and injured hundreds.\n- During the Trial of Dzhokhar Tsarnaev, Judy Clarke also said that Dzhokhar Tsarnaev and Tamerlan Tsarnaev murdered an MIT police officer days later.",
